-- title:
--   The subfield $\mathbb F(f)\subseteq\mathbb F(x)$ generated by polynomials
-- statement:
--   For polynomials $h_1,h_2,\dots\in\mathbb F[x_1,\dots,x_n]$, $\mathbb F[h]$ is the $\mathbb F$-algebra they generate and $\mathbb F(h)$ its fraction field, realised as the smallest subfield of $\mathbb F(x)$ that contains $\mathbb F$ and every $h_i$.
--
--   For an intermediate field $E$ and $\gamma\in\mathbb F(x)$, $E(\gamma)$ is the smallest subfield containing $E$ and $\gamma$, and $[K:E]$ denotes the dimension of $K$ as an $E$-vector space.
--
--   These are the fields in the tower $\mathbb F(f)\subseteq\mathbb F(f,x_{i_1})\subseteq\cdots\subseteq\mathbb F(x)$ studied in §4.3.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `adjoinFamily h` is `IntermediateField.adjoin F` of the images of the $h_i$ in $\mathbb F(x)$. In the theorems, $E(\gamma)$ is `IntermediateField.adjoin E {γ}` and $[K:E]$ is `Module.rank E K`, a cardinal, so a bound $[K:E]\le N$ with $N\in\mathbb N$ also asserts that the extension is finite.
-- source:
--   Forbes and Staicu, Approximating Transcendence Degree in Medium Characteristic, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 3ab72a42…), §2.1, p.7; Definition 2.2, p.7

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TrDegJac_RatFn

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace TrDegJac

/-- **The subfield `F(f)` of `F(x)` generated by a family of polynomials** — Forbes and Staicu,
*Approximating Transcendence Degree in Medium Characteristic*, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript
sha256 3ab72a42…), §2.1, p.7: "For any collection of polynomials f₁, …, f_m ∈ F[x] we write F[f] for
the F-algebra generated by the polynomials f₁, …, f_m, and we denote its fraction field by F(f)."

**Formalization Note.** `F(f)` is realized as the intermediate field of `F ⊆ F(x)` generated by the
images of the `f_i`; it is the fraction field of `F[f]` inside `F(x)`. Adjoining further elements
`γ` to an intermediate field `E` (the paper's `E(γ)`, e.g. `F(f, x_i)` over `F(f)`) is written
`IntermediateField.adjoin E {γ}`. Field degrees `[K : E]` are `Module.rank E K`, a cardinal, so a
bound `[K : E] ≤ N` also asserts that the extension is finite. -/
noncomputable def adjoinFamily {F : Type*} [Field F] {n : ℕ} {ι : Type*}
    (h : ι → MvPolynomial (Fin n) F) : IntermediateField F (RatFn F n) :=
  IntermediateField.adjoin F (Set.range fun i => toRatFn (h i))

end TrDegJac


